#: ../../../users/foldermaster.rst:4
msgid "Folder Master Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/foldermaster.rst:6
msgid "A folder can be set in \"master mode\" among the folder settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/foldermaster.rst:10
msgid ""
"The intention is for this to be used on devices where a \"master copy\" of "
"files are kept - where the files are not expected to be changed on other "
"devices or where such changes would be undesirable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/foldermaster.rst:14
msgid ""
"In master mode, all changes from other devices in the cluster are ignored. "
"Changes are still *received* so the folder may become \"out of sync\", but "
"no changes will be applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/foldermaster.rst:18
msgid ""
"When a master folder becomes out of sync, a red \"Override Changes\" button "
"is shown at the bottom of the folder details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/foldermaster.rst:23
msgid ""
"Clicking this button will enforce the master's current state on the rest of "
"the cluster. Any changes made to files will be overwritten by the version on "
"the master, any files that don't exist on the master will be deleted, and so "
"on."
msgstr ""
